{{!--
  Shot-pattern RESOLUTION card (CP2020 p.109) — one card for the whole burst, however many shells it
  threw. Rendered via renderTemplate with
  { weaponName, band, shells, multiShell, dmgFormula, rows: [{ name, rolls, total, breakdown }] }.
  `rolls` is the per-shell damage list as text, so N shells read as N numbers rather than as one sum.
  Rows are DIVs, not a list: core's own layered `ul` styling wins over a module rule on this build
  (probed — list-style computed `circle` with the module rule live), and a chat card wants no markers.
  i18n via CPLocal; triple-stash where the string carries <b>.

  ⭐ `breakdown` (2026-08-28, ruling A) is the COLLAPSED per-figure math the Apply window's own line
  shows, built by the same renderer from the rows the apply actually produced — see the partial and
  combat/damage-breakdown.js. Absent on a row whose apply produced none, in which case the card is
  byte-identical to the one that shipped before.
--}}
<div class="cyberpunk save-prompt">
  <h3>{{CPLocal "SpreadResultTitle" weapon=weaponName}}</h3>
  <div class="save-info">
    {{#if multiShell}}
      <span>{{{CPLocal "SpreadResultSummaryShells" shells=shells band=band dmg=dmgFormula}}}</span>
    {{else}}
      <span>{{{CPLocal "SpreadResultSummary" band=band dmg=dmgFormula}}}</span>
    {{/if}}
    <div class="cp-spread-result-list">
      {{#each rows}}
        <div class="cp-spread-result-row">{{{CPLocal "SpreadResultRow" name=this.name rolls=this.rolls total=this.total}}}</div>
        {{#if this.breakdown}}{{> "modules/cp2020-augmented/templates/chat/parts/area-breakdown.hbs" breakdown=this.breakdown}}{{/if}}
      {{/each}}
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
